{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["And the sense of <b>And YHWH put a matter in the mouth of Balaam</b> — some commentators explain that Balaam did not know the matters himself, but HaShem filled him with the words and said to him: \"Return to Balak and thus shall you speak,\" for the words will come out of your mouth. And perhaps this is also the view of our Sages, who said (Tanchuma, Balak 12): He bent his mouth and formed it like a person who drives a peg into a board. Rabbi Eliezer says: an angel was speaking; Rabbi Yehoshua says, etc. But this is not correct in my eyes, because he said: \"hearing the sayings of El, who sees a vision of Shaddai\" (Numbers 24:4). Rather, the sense of <b>and He put</b> — it is a teaching: He taught him the words so that he would rattle them off in his mouth and not forget and not drop a single word from them, in the sense of \"and teach it to the children of Israel, put it in their mouth\" (Deuteronomy 31:19), and likewise \"for by the mouth of Absalom was the counsel established\" (II Samuel 13:32)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:08:03.593328535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}